Vendored third-party code
=========================

okf-validate.mjs, okf-graph.mjs
  Source:  https://github.com/Sudhakaran88/okf-conformance
  License: MIT — Copyright (c) 2026 WitsCode (see LICENSE in this directory)

These are the Open Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2 conformance validator and graph
renderer from the okf-conformance project, vendored so that `okf_check.sh` runs
without a network fetch or a separate install.

Two local modifications are applied on top of the upstream files. Both live in
the shared `extractLinks` / `stripCode` helpers of each file:

1. Percent-decoding of link destinations. CommonMark §6.6 (RFC 3986) allows a
   link to a file named `a b.md` to be written `a%20b.md`. Upstream resolved
   the raw destination against the filesystem, so every filename containing a
   space read as a broken link.

2. Ignoring links inside fenced code blocks and code spans. Documentation about
   markdown embeds example links in fences constantly; counting those produced
   phantom unresolved-link warnings. `stripCode()` blanks code regions (keeping
   line count and length) before link extraction.

Both changes keep the upstream conformance fixtures passing. They are candidates
for an upstream pull request; until one lands, they are carried here.
